      ("Which sources AI answers cite",
       "<p>Pew also looked at the links shown in AI summaries. The vast majority, 88%, cited three or more sources, and only 1% cited a single source. Wikipedia, YouTube and Reddit were the most commonly linked sites, together accounting for 15% of sources in AI summaries and 17% in standard results. Government websites made up 6% of AI summary sources, compared with 2% of standard results, while news sites made up 5% of both.</p><p>For a business, the takeaway is that AI summaries usually draw on several pages, and third-party platforms like Reddit and YouTube are a large part of the mix. Being the best page on your own site is necessary, but being mentioned elsewhere helps too.</p>"),
